yid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"001911a76e69cead434fe78f195bf116e5fc9aff36e80997531dab03b205d404","event_uuid":"63201393-7b22-4427-aa51-8220f216926b","position":{"commit_sha":"87ccfa7ba38f4fa0ff0918483e6b9f66e0e56349","position":"1786560592772243001-63201393-7b22-4427-aa51-8220f216926b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC3 — OPERATOR ACTION, not an agent change: the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repository secret is absent. Run 31587452003's anthropic arm failed its credential preflight with `::error title=anthropic arm has no credential::Set the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY repository secret`. Adding it requires GitHub repo Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions, which an agent cannot reach — it needs a repository admin.\n\nThe arm's fail-not-skip design is CORRECT and is deliberately unchanged by this ticket's change (Gerrit 1658). The preflight exits non-zero rather than letting the arm skip every llm_live test and report green; the `llm-live-canary` in tests/external/conftest.py is the second, independent defence for the same failure mode (collected>0, executed=0 => exit 1). Do not soften either.\n\nRelated but out of scope, filed separately: the OIDC credential step stays gated to the bedrock arm, so a bedrock-pinned module on the anthropic/openai arms may now fail on AWS *credentials* where it previously failed on region. That is a distinct defect from this ticket's region-resolution signature.","timestamp":1786558251052688001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC3 UPDATE — operator action COMPLETE (supersedes the 'pending' framing in the previous AC3 comment).\n\nThe operator reports the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repository secret has been rotated/added in both places: locally, and as a GitHub Actions secret on this repository. (`JIRA_API_TOKEN` was rotated earlier, separately.) No secret values were handled or recorded by the agent; this note records the fact of the action only.\n\nSo the anthropic arm's credential preflight — which failed run 31587452003 with `::error title=anthropic arm has no credential::` — now has the secret it requires. AC3 is therefore satisfied on both halves: the gap was recorded as an operator action, that action is done, and the arm's fail-not-skip design is unchanged by Gerrit 1658 (the change touches only the region env, plus a doc note and a regression test).","timestamp":1786560017134064001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI triage (Verified -1 on patch set 1, run 31626336603): NOT caused by this change. Single failure was tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py::test_main_without_repo_root_passes_resolved_repo_root (1 failed, 12327 passed, macos-latest/py3.13) — a test-isolation defect where main() returns early via ReconcileGateError on the runner's corrupt refs/reconciler/gate before check_pass_lock is reached. Filed as brown-caring-weasel (discovered_from this ticket) with the confirmed mechanism; posted 'recheck' on 1658. The file passes locally: 13 passed.","timestamp":1786560592772243001}],"created_at":1786533661537838001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"36d64eb7-abbd-445f-9965-66d781ec2e8c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4ad9-34cb-c6d2-49e9"}],"description":"# Context\n\nLive External Integration run 31587452003 (operator-sanctioned dispatch) failed both\nlive-LLM arms (anthropic + openai) on two pure-configuration causes.\n\n## Cause 1 — region is exported only on the bedrock arm (confirmed mechanism)\n\n`.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` L202-203 (origin/main) guard BOTH region\nvars on the arm:\n\n    AWS_DEFAULT_REGION: ${{ matrix.provider == 'bedrock' && vars.AWS_BEDROCK_CI_REGION || '' }}\n    REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION: ${{ matrix.provider == 'bedrock' && vars.AWS_BEDROCK_CI_REGION || '' }}\n\nOn the anthropic and openai arms both evaluate to the empty string. But\n`tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py:32` pins\n`_MODEL = \"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\"` — a bedrock-routed model\n*regardless of which arm runs it*. So every 0707 cell on a non-bedrock arm hits\n`build_bedrock_provider` with no resolvable region and raises the typed\n`LLMConfigError` naming `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION`. A region is not a credential\n(it is a repository *variable*, per the file's own preflight comment), so the\nper-arm guard buys no credential isolation here — it only starves arms that run\nbedrock-pinned modules.\n\n## Cause 2 — ANTHROPIC_API_KEY repository secret missing\n\nThe anthropic arm emits `::error title=anthropic arm has no credential::`. Adding the\nsecret is an OPERATOR action (repo settings). The arm's fail-not-skip design is CORRECT\nand must not be changed.\n\n# Plan\n\n1. `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` L202-203: drop the\n   `matrix.provider == 'bedrock' &&` guard from both region vars and give them a\n   literal `us-east-1` fallback, so every arm resolves a region:\n   `${{ vars.AWS_BEDROCK_CI_REGION || 'us-east-1' }}`. `us-east-1` is rebar's\n   documented Bedrock region (`docs/llm-framework.md:182`,\n   `docs/calibration/overlap_batch_confidence.md:10`).\n   Update the adjacent comment block (L194-201) to say why the region is now\n   unguarded: live-LLM modules may pin a `bedrock:` model on any arm.\n2. `docs/ci-provider-matrix.md` §\"Bedrock: region is a separate, mandatory setting\":\n   the text says \"The arm sets both …\", which becomes stale. One sentence: the region\n   is set on EVERY arm because bedrock-pinned modules run on all of them.\n3. Comment on this ticket recording the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret as an operator action.\n\nOut of scope: the fail-not-skip credential design; AWS credential (OIDC) availability on\nnon-bedrock arms — the OIDC step stays guarded on `matrix.provider == 'bedrock'`, so a\nbedrock-pinned cell on the anthropic arm may still fail on *credentials*. That is a\ndistinct defect and gets its own `discovered_from` ticket rather than being folded in\nhere; this ticket's AC2 is scoped to the region-resolution signature only.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION` (and `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`) are exported for the\n  live-LLM suite step on every matrix arm, resolving to `us-east-1` when\n  `vars.AWS_BEDROCK_CI_REGION` is unset.\n- [ ] AC2 — The 0707 banking cells no longer fail on region resolution (evidence: run\n  link, or `[operator-attested]` citing run 31587452003's failure signature + the env diff).\n- [ ] AC3 — A comment records that adding the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repository secret is an\n  operator action, and that the arm's fail-not-skip design is correct and unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"export REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION/AWS_DEFAULT_REGION on every live-LLM matrix arm, defaulting to us-east-1"},{"path":"docs/ci-provider-matrix.md","reason":"the region section said the bedrock arm sets the vars; note it is now set on every arm"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py","reason":"regression test: the region env must not be guarded on matrix.provider and must carry a fallback"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4ad9-34cb-c6d2-49e9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"df199b57-a6df-47f8-822a-1dc90eb23d3e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"79d6-7e6e-e1c0-4c20","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live-LLM external lane fails on unset bedrock region; anthropic arm lacks secret","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9b1e7638-2e42-4e92-bf64-c86a21ead542","c3f50ebd-6f81-44d8-af63-26e83b0a3531","613b8bab-438b-4709-854a-f62de057f722","8f8c7219-60e6-4032-99bd-62582ee0ad02","df199b57-a6df-47f8-822a-1dc90eb23d3e","4a032f69-45f1-4332-a588-b8b40ebb9f82","f846d901-dcc6-4787-b93f-43a44a5e61e6","fedf40a7-9da4-442b-a01d-11ccf92cc2fd","36d64eb7-abbd-445f-9965-66d781ec2e8c","ec315c71-8fe8-4778-871c-80ebfd2fd1e1","63201393-7b22-4427-aa51-8220f216926b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786560592772243002,"uuid":"93cc0114-88e3-4033-bcf7-b6b78bfade1e"}